<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zanticus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 175 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zanticus was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iazyges">Iazyges</a>, a Sarmatian people of the Hungarian plain, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcomannic-wars">Marcomannic Wars</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> defeated his people, he made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-aurelius">Marcus Aurelius</a> in 175, returning tens of thousands of Roman captives and providing 8,000 cavalry, of whom 5,500 were sent to serve in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p></div>
